    "Liberal-feminist, Rawlsian, feminist-political-liberal, feminist-jurisprudential, and socially grounded autonomy scholarship supports testing the public and institutional conditions required for meaningful personal and political autonomy and equal opportunity, rather than reducing the branch to formal rights, welfare support, or one policy instrument.",
